.\" No version in the title line. A man page that names one has to be edited at
.\" every release for a line nobody reads, and the version that matters is the
.\" one the binary prints.
.TH IRONTILE 1 "" "irontile" "irontile"
.SH NAME
irontile \- a Wayland tiling compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B irontile
.RB [ \-\-session | \-\-nested | \-\-headless
.RI [ SPEC ]]
.RB [ \-\-wayland\-display
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B irontile \-\-print\-config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B irontile
is a Wayland compositor whose native model is a tree of split containers rather
than a floating desktop with tiling bolted on. Windows are placed by the tree;
nothing overlaps unless it is asked to float.
.PP
It is normally started by a login manager through the session entry, which runs
.BR start\-irontile (1)
rather than this binary directly, so that a crash is restarted instead of
ending the session.
.PP
With no backend named, irontile nests if
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
or
.B DISPLAY
is set and takes the session otherwise, which is what each of those situations
means.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-session
Drive real hardware through DRM. The default when there is no compositor
already running to nest in.
.TP
.B \-\-nested
Run as a window inside the compositor already running. The default when there
is one.
.TP
.BR \-\-headless " [" \fISPEC\fR ]
Run without a renderer, with displays described by
.IR SPEC :
a comma\-separated list of
.I WxH
or
.IR WxH+X+Y ,
defaulting to one 1920x1080 display. For tests, and for driving irontile purely
over its control socket.
.TP
.BI \-\-wayland\-display " NAME"
Bind this Wayland socket name instead of picking the first free one. Useful
when the name has to be known in advance, such as on a machine where another
compositor already holds
.BR wayland\-1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.I PATH
instead of the usual place.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Write the default configuration to standard output and exit. Every default
binding, as the text a user would write.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit. A running compositor is asked its own version by
.BR "irontilectl version" ,
which is not always the one installed.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/irontile/irontile.toml
Configuration. Falls back to
.IR ~/.config/irontile/irontile.toml .
A missing file is not an error: it means the defaults.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/irontile/<display>.sock
The control socket, keyed by Wayland display name so that two compositors on
one machine do not collide. See
.BR irontilectl (1).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/irontile/irontile.log
What a session wrote, with the run before it kept as
.IR irontile.log.1 ,
five deep. Nested and headless runs do not write it: they are started from a
terminal somebody is already watching.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
.B irontile=debug
logs displays lighting, each reflow's placements, and keypresses that hold a
modifier or fire a binding.
.B irontile=trace
adds the page\-flip cycle, which is two lines per frame per display. Plain
typing is never logged at any level, and neither are window titles, spawn
arguments or clipboard contents: turning on debug logging must not turn the
compositor into a keylogger.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-irontile (1),
.BR irontilectl (1),
.BR irontile\-bar (1),
.BR irontile\-lock (1),
.BR irontile\-polkit (1)
.PP
The README in the source distribution is the long form of all of this.
